  "notes": [
    {
      "marker": "1.",
      "text": "PSYC courses at 2000 and above level will be included in the calculation of Major GPA for honours classification.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "2.",
      "text": "A Psychology Major student who pursues a second Major in Linguistics can be exempted from taking LING3403 and LING3202 by taking PSYC2010 and PSYC3430 respectively. Units earned can be counted towards both Major Programmes.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[a]",
      "text": "Students are required to take PSYC2010. Students who have transferred to the Psychology Programme and have taken any of the equivalent statistics courses including COMM3110, DOTE2011, ECON2121, GRMD2102, LING3403, PHPC2015, SEEM2430, SOCI2004, SPED2600, STAT2001 and 2006, STAT2101 and 2102 are exempted from taking PSYC2010, and they are required to take another PSYC (2000 or above level) course listed under 3. Elective Courses to compensate for the units.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "[b]",
      "text": "Students are required to take PSYC2540. Students who have transferred to the Psychology Programme and have taken SOWK2110 or SOWK2120 or EDUC2310 will be exempted from taking PSYC2540, and they are required to take another PSYC (2000 or above level) course listed under 3. Elective Courses to compensate for the units.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    }
  ],
